\section{Quadrature}{

Method \code{"quadrature"} alternates between placing the nodes around the
modes at the current parameters and one trust step over every parameter
on these frozen nodes, with the exact Hessian where the model has second
derivatives. The nodes of the mu-referenced fixed effects (random
intercepts whose formula covers every condition with data, covariates
constant within a group) are frozen in \verb{phi = X beta + eta}, so these
fixed effects need no sensitivities between two rebuilds. Entries of
\code{control$quadrature}:
\describe{
\item{\code{tol}}{allowed change of -2 log L by the next level, default 0.1,
split evenly over the groups: each group takes the lowest level from
its stage up whose next level changes its -2 log L by at most
\code{tol / G}, and never a lower level than before. \code{Inf} keeps the levels
of the stages.}
\item{\code{levels}}{the stages, default \code{K + 1} with \code{K} the number of random
effects of a group; level \code{K + s} integrates polynomials of total
degree \verb{2 s + 1} exactly.}
\item{\code{maxLevel}}{highest level, default \code{K + 8}.}
\item{\code{tolDecrement}}{a stage ends when a Newton step on the rebuilt
nodes would lower -2 log L by less than \code{tolDecrement}, default 1e-4,
or than the nodes resolve, the change of -2 log L by the next level
summed over the groups; or by less than the last step raised it on
rebuilt nodes of the same levels, at its iterate of lowest -2 log L.
Each counts as converged.}
\item{\code{maxEcmPerStage}, \code{cm1Control}, \code{maxCm1Iter}}{rebuilds per stage
(default 10), \code{\link[=trust]{trust()}} settings and iterations of a step (default 30).}
\item{\code{pruneTol}}{nodes whose weight lies this much in log below the
largest are dropped, default \code{Inf}.}
\item{\code{certificate}}{\code{FALSE}, or a list of \code{points} (default 256) and
\code{seed} (default 1) of the importance-sampling check at the estimate: a
multivariate t5 proposal at the mode and conditional covariance of each
group, randomly shifted lattice points. A group is flagged when the two
-2 log L differ by more than three standard errors plus the error its
level allows (the larger of \code{tol / G} and its estimated level error),
or when the Pareto shape of the weights exceeds 0.7.}
}
Method \code{"laplaceEM"} reads \code{epsEcm} (default 1e-5), the extrapolated
distance of the parameters to the fixed point at which it stops, \code{maxEcm},
\code{cm1Control} and \code{maxCm1Iter}.
}

\examples{
\donttest{
## Theophylline, 12 subjects: one-compartment oral model, log parameters with a normal
## random intercept per subject, additive error
library(dMod2)
outdir <- tempdir()
data(Theoph, package = "datasets")
Theoph$Subject <- as.character(Theoph$Subject)
subjects <- sort(unique(Theoph$Subject))
data <- as.datalist(data.frame(name = "y", time = Theoph$Time, value = Theoph$conc,
                               sigma = NA_real_, condition = Theoph$Subject))

reactions <- eqnlist()
reactions <- addReaction(reactions, "Ag", "",   "Ka * Ag",     "absorption")
reactions <- addReaction(reactions, "",   "Cc", "Ka * Ag / V", "appearance")
reactions <- addReaction(reactions, "Cc", "",   "Cl/V * Cc",   "elimination")
x <- Xs(odemodel(reactions, modelname = "theoph_ode", compile = FALSE, deriv2 = TRUE,
                 outdir = outdir))
g <- Y(c(y = "Cc"), x, modelname = "theoph_obs", compile = FALSE, deriv2 = TRUE, outdir = outdir)
err <- Y(eqnvec(y = "sigma_add"), g, attachInput = FALSE, modelname = "theoph_err",
         compile = FALSE, deriv2 = TRUE, outdir = outdir)

## one condition per subject, the dose from the branch table; the effect formula
## replaces each log parameter by its intercept plus a random effect per subject
doses <- tapply(Theoph$Dose * Theoph$Wt, Theoph$Subject, `[`, 1)[subjects]
trafo <- branch(define(NULL, "x <- x", x = c("Ka", "V", "Cl", "Ag", "Cc", "sigma_add")),
                table = data.frame(ID = subjects, dose = doses, row.names = subjects))
trafo <- insert(trafo, "Ag <- dose", dose = dose)
trafo <- insert(trafo, "Cc <- 0")
trafo <- insert(trafo, "x <- exp(x)", x = c("Ka", "V", "Cl", "sigma_add"))
trafo <- insert(trafo, Ka + V + Cl ~ 1 + (1 | ID))
p <- P(trafo, method = "explicit", compile = FALSE, modelname = "theoph_p", deriv2 = TRUE,
       outdir = outdir)
compile(x, g, err, p, output = "theoph_nlme")

obj <- normL2(data, g * x * p, errmodel = err)
fit <- em(obj, randomEffects(p), init = c(Ka = 0, V = 3, Cl = 0.7, sigma_add = log(0.5)))
summary(fit)
fit$omega
head(fit$random)
head(residuals(fit, type = "CWRES"))
confint(fit, parm = "Cl", method = "profile")

## diagnostics: residuals, NPDE from simulations, a visual predictive check, the random
## effects against the body weight of the subjects
npde <- residuals(fit, type = "NPDE", nsim = 200, seed = 1)
attr(npde, "tests")
plotResiduals(fit, nsim = 200, seed = 1)
plotVPC(fit, nsim = 100, bins = 6, seed = 1)
weight <- tapply(Theoph$Wt, Theoph$Subject, `[`, 1)[subjects]
plotRandomEffects(fit, covariates = data.frame(weight = weight, row.names = subjects))

## four starts
best <- msem(obj, randomEffects(p), init = c(Ka = 0, V = 3, Cl = 0.7, sigma_add = log(0.5)),
             fits = 4)
best$multistart
}
}
